  "releaseNotes": "LC025 (Avoid AsNoTracking with Update/Remove) is now path-aware for conditionally reassigned locals. When the latest assignment before the write sits in a branch that may not execute and the latest unconditional fallback disagrees on tracking-ness, the entity's state depends on the path taken and the rule stays quiet instead of judging by the lexically-last write. Unconditional latest assignments, agreeing fallbacks (every path untracked), superseded history, and same-branch reassign-plus-write shapes all keep firing.",
